<title>CHINA: Freight load factor of AAPA airlines up 7.56 pct.</title>
<headline>Freight load factor of AAPA airlines up 7.56 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The freight load factor of airlines belonging to the Association of Asia Pacific Airlines (AAPA) rose by a record 7.56 per cent in March.</p>
<p>Monthly statistics of member airlines, detailed in AAPA's Orient aviation magazine, showed cargo maintained double digit growth exceeding capacity growth leading to a 4.35 percent climb in April's freight load factor</p>
<p>AAPA, formerly the Orient Airlines Association, has 18 members in the Asia Pacific region including Cathay Pacific Airways Limited, China Airlines, Japan Airlines, Singapore Airlines and Qantas Airways.</p>
<p>Passenger traffic rose by 7.3 per cent in March and 9.3 percent in April but passenger load factors for both months was slightly down on the corresponding period in 1996 reflecting the measure of passenger capacity, Available Seat Kilometres (ASK's), exceeding Revenue Passenger Kilometres(RPKs).</p>
